<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49774" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰαύω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῐ]</span>, poet. Verb, mostly used in
			pres. and impf. (Trag. only in lyr.): 
			Ep.
		
		impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰαύεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.184
				</span></i>
			, Perdrizet-Lefebvre <i>Graffītes Grecs du
				Memnonion d' Abydos</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				528
			</span></i>: fut.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰαύσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					101
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				430
			</span></i>: aor. 1
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴαυσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.261
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.</u>
				3.1.2
			</span></i>:—<i>sleep, pass the night</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζηνὸς . . ἐν ἀγκοίνῃσιν ἰαύεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					14.213
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				11.261
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀΰπνους νύκτας ἴαυον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.325
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				19.340
			</span></i>; of beasts, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθα δὲ πολλὰ μῆλ᾽ . . ἰαύεσκον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.184
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρσενες ἐκτὸς ἴαυον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					14.16
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δεμνίοις δύστανος ἰαύων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1537
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): c. acc. cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐννυχίαν
				τέρψιν ἰαύειν</span>
			<i>enjoy</i> the night's sleep, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				1204
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπασπίδιον κοῖτον
			ἰαύειν</span>, of a soldier <i>sleeping</i> under arms, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				740
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					3.49
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
			</span></i> l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.
			et gen., <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				101
			</span></i>. (Prob. redupl. form of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὔω</span> (c), cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄω</span> (A) <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλή</span>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
